  "result_text": "`GET /members/{memberId}/loans/history` is in place and committed as `34c747c` on `feat/loan-limit`. `./gradlew build` passes, including the 4 new integration tests.\n\nEach item has `loanId`, `title`, `loanedAt`, `returnedAt` and `lateFee`, newest loan first. Returned loans are included. Unreturned loans have `returnedAt` and `lateFee` set to `null`. A member with no loans gets `[]`, and an unknown member gets 404.\n\nDecisions I made that you didn't specify:\n- **Ties on `loanedAt`:** broken by `id` descending, so the order is deterministic.\n- **On-time returns:** `lateFee` is `0`, not `null`. `null` only means \"not returned yet\".\n- **No paging:** the endpoint returns the full history as a plain array, as your example shows. The existing active-loans endpoint is paged, so say if you want this one paged too.\n\nThe changes follow the existing layering: a new method on `GetMemberLoansUseCase`, a new `LoadLoanPort` method backed by a Spring Data query, and a response record in `adapter.in.web`. The new endpoint reuses the existing title lookup.",
